From 15b40b8ad608d6eef1b09801e6890990f3856f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:13:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] board: samsung: add the Galaxy S8+ (dream2lte)

U-Boot as the kernel of the boot image in BOOT, chainloaded by S-Boot
(which loads it at a random address: position independent).

- display: the bootloader framebuffer, kept refreshing (DECON trigger)
- UFS, extlinux from the USERDATA partition; the kernel DT keeps its
  memory node (no EFI, no memory fixup)
- keys: boot menu on Volume Down, Bixby held 5 s reboots into TWRP
- USB: fastboot, mass storage, CDC ACM; the MAX77865 MUIC is switched
  to the SoC over HSI2C_32 (USI13 put in I2C mode)
- reboot into S-Boot's modes (reboot recovery/download), fastboot
  reboot reasons
- chainload: the original kernel of a boot image carried after U-Boot
  (tools/d2l-bootimg.py), entered as S-Boot would
- console mirrored into the ramoops zone (no reachable UART), read back
  from TWRP or Linux pstore

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
